# Local data, never published: every folder whose name starts with an underscore. _data is the
# local data folder (the free sources, their readings, the measurements), _sources the original
# books (the commercial ones above all), _work everything the pipeline keeps on this machine, the
# reading of the commercial books included, _internal_archive the internal documents.
# One wrong rule here would publish them with the next push, so a contract test holds it.
/_*/
_*/

# The data's places before it moved to _data/: ignored, so nothing written there is ever published.
/corpus/raw/
/corpus/readings/
/evaluation/results/

# This machine's own settings, laid over configs/app_config.json (decision 285.a).
/configs/*.local.json

# Developer tooling: its settings, rules and skills live in .claude/.
# CLAUDE.md is named as well as a safety net, so a copy anywhere else in the tree stays out too.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
.claude.json
.mcp.json

# Keys and credentials, should one ever land here: keys belong in .env
claude-key*.json
*-key.json
*.key
*.pem
id_rsa*
keys/
secrets/
.envrc
.env.*
!.env.example

# Internal working notes and drafts
INTERNAL_*
/ISSUE_*.md
/JOBS_*.md
/SESSION_*.md
/HANDOFF_*.md
SUMMARY_*.md
export_github_issues.sh

# Local databases; everything built from the corpus (vector store, SQLite) is derived and rebuilt by
# the pipeline.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
corpus/index/

# Virtual environments (the RAGAS report has its own: requirements-eval.txt) and tool caches
.venv/
.venv-eval/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Secrets — secrets.example.json / .env.example ARE tracked as templates.
# Path-independent on purpose: the RAG sprint's layout is not decided yet.
**/secrets.json
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# What the editable install of this project writes
*.egg-info/
build/

# Runtime artefacts
# The turn log (phase 10): every question, prompt and passage of every turn; local only.
logs/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
# The diagnostics UI's build IS tracked, so a reviewer needs no Node; a contract test holds it current.
!src/frontend/diagnostics/dist/
playwright-report/
test-results/
coverage/

# Editor settings
.vscode/
# The operator's VS Code workspace names local folders beside this repository (untracked since 26 Nov 2026)
*.code-workspace
